  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What is the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{8}{x-6}-7\\,?$\n\nThe range is\n$f(x)\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\cup (${{field-3}}$,\\infty ).$",
  "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=-7.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-7,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-7)\\cup (-7,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14094369/assets/3a4220e6f7375a1c8afa30d9c6ada276bc945e304b9538bb455ba7cb2738053f.png)",
